= Maintenance

Your FujiNet cartridge should bring many years of enjoyment. To keep it in
good working condition, please remember the following points:

- Always turn the POWER switch on the console OFF before putting the
  cartridge in or taking it out.
- Don't try to force the cartridge into the console.
- Don't push anything into the three small service holes on the back of the
  cartridge.
- Push the memory card straight in and let it spring straight out. Don't pry
  at it.
- Use only a USB-C phone charger or a computer's USB port in the USB-C socket.
- Don't spill liquids on the cartridge or pour them into the console's slot.
- Don't drop the cartridge or leave it in great heat.
- Clean the outside of the cartridge with a soft, slightly damp cloth.

== Keeping FujiNet Up to Date

FujiNet's firmware -- the programs inside the cartridge -- is improved all the
time. New versions, and how to load them, are announced at *fujinet.online*.
Loading new firmware does not change your hosts or your WiFi settings.
